#1507
The Pilgrim's Vow~
   Words are cut into the rock here in a flowing hand, the vow that Oswen
the First Pilgrim made at this spot: to walk straight though the road is
hard, to carry the light though it burns the hand, and to answer for all he
carried when he came to be weighed. Every penitent says it aloud before
going on, and after it, everything carried this far seems light. Ways lead
east and west, and a stair goes down.
~
