#1514
The Fall~
   In the beginning Sefhra was the first and fairest of the Watchers of the
Road. When the Weigher set the scales upon the road, every Watcher bowed and
laid a hand on them to be weighed first. Sefhra would not; nothing so fair,
he said, could be found wanting. Look at your own beauty, pilgrim, and do
what he could not: put it on the scales. The hall runs north and south.
~
